WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.970
- All right, everybody.

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:02.760
Let's wrap things up with one last story

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.210
to bring you joy, hopefully.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.112
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:07.695
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.750
Like I mentioned earlier,

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.070
today kicks off Women's History Month.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.300
To celebrate, I want you
to meet a 19 year old

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.270
from Belgium who just made
history as the youngest woman

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.510
to fly solo around the world.

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.060
In fact, she broke the
two Guinness world records

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:22.893
on the journey.

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:24.910
It took her five months traveling

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.020
through 41 countries across 32,300 miles.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.978
Geez, let's say hi to Zara.

00:00:31.978 --> 00:00:33.967
(audience cheering)

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.170
Hi, Zara!

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.220
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.030
- Oh my god, this is a tremendous feat!

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.070
So why you wanna do it?

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.140
- So I'd always thought
flying around the world,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.480
it would just be the coolest thing

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.480
like the most amazing adventure.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.260
I'm really lucky both
my parents are pilots.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.770
So I grew up around aviation
but I always assumed

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.030
that it'd be too dangerous,
too complicated, too expensive.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.370
So I never really thought about it.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.530
And then I was finishing high school

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.610
and I think that's when I realized

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.470
with that attitude I'm not going anywhere.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.430
So I said, "I'm doing
this a hundred percent."

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.380
So I planned my route,
grabbed a pen and a world map

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.230
and kind of drew a line around the world

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.230
where I wanted to go.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.750
And then spent ages
looking for sponsorship,

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.460
emailed 500 companies.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.030
They basically all said no

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.270
but then a Bulgarian
man phoned me up one day

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.900
and he said, "Zara, how are you doing?"

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.270
And, "I wanna help you out."

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.590
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:23.770
See it hit home with somebody.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.603
That's really cool.

00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:25.820
So it was quite a journey

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.110
but you faced many setbacks, right?

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:28.943
- I did.

00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:30.220
So I left in August

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.770
and it was supposed to take three months

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.500
but it actually took five
months and it was pretty tough.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.333
Amazing.

00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:39.410
Flying over Iceland I think
was the most incredible moment

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.300
when I saw an active
volcano from the plane.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.950
Then the hardest moment

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.100
for me was probably
flying over California.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.820
At the time, there were
some pretty bad wildfires

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.393
and it got to a point
where I was flying along

00:01:51.393 --> 00:01:54.050
and I could just smell
the smoke in the cockpit

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.800
and not see a single thing
because it was just so heavy.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.060
And later on the toughest
moment was definitely Siberia

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:01.990
for me.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.950
I was flying in minus
31 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.910
I was super, super remote
and just really intimidating

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.350
because if the engine quit,
suddenly I'm stuck hours away

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.270
from rescue in a really cold climate.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.650
But it was incredible,
the people were amazing

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.870
and I couldn't have asked
for a better opportunity.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.930
- That's awesome.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.880
What a cool adventure that you went on.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.880
I mean, this would make an
amazing movie, just saying.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.280
Thank you so much Zara.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.760
Continue success in the aviation field!

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.263
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:33.563
That's not all though.

00:02:33.563 --> 00:02:35.750
I wanna tell you our season
long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.480
makers of G2, the go to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.750
want to honor ultimate
overachiever like you.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.170
I can't imagine actually anybody better

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.320
to give this money to.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.440
So they're gonna write
you a check for $1000.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.318
How's that sound?

00:02:47.318 --> 00:02:51.270
(audience cheering drowns out Zara)

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.400
All right. All right.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.312
- Thank you.

00:02:53.312 --> 00:02:55.530
- Hey, if you ever, if you
ever wanna do another cool trip

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.100
like that hit me up, I'll help you out.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.380
That's so cool what you're doing.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.040
I just wanna see the pictures from it.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.675
Thank you so much.

00:03:01.675 --> 00:03:04.228
- Thank you. You can be
the passenger in the back.

00:03:04.228 --> 00:03:06.478
- [Kelly Clarkson] All
right, good luck Zara!

